      "message": "Don\u0027t you need to make a copy of mBaseIface under the lock?\n\nIn fact, I think the locking requirements would be more clear if there were an inner class like this:\n\n    private static class InternalState {\n        public String baseIface;\n        public String iface;\n        public boolean isRunning;\n\n        public InternalState(InternalState other) {\n            ...copy constructor...\n        }\n\n        public void setBaseInterface(String baseIface) {\n            this.baseIface \u003d baseIface;\n            this.iface \u003d CLAT_PREFIX + this.baseIface;\n        }\n\n        public boolean isStarted() {\n            return (iface !\u003d null);\n        }\n\n        public void clear() {\n            baseIface \u003d null;\n            iface \u003d null;\n            isRunning \u003d false;\n        }\n    }\n\nThen it should be clear that any time the (now final!) mInternalState variable gets accessed we lock on it, if only long enough to create a copy to work after exiting the locked section.\n\nToo much?",
