      "message": "mBaseIface is set by start() which is call on ConnectivityService thread and cannot overlap with stop() which is also called there, so that side is good.\n\nmBaseIface is also nulled by interfaceRemoved(), which is called by NMS, but as a result of mNMService.stopClatd(). So here mBaseIface cannot be nulled yet.\n\nI thought about the usage of an inner data class for representing the state. That class could then be grabbed safely with volatile. But then I thought it might be a bit overkill. Maybe I can actually do it.",
